{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295703Z","id":"7b5c5fd02200e74ac2224fc033f85d93517f02ed07fe0c118d991bf0277308eb","body":{"detail":"main.ts appends tokens.css as a <style> element, and vite.overlay.config.ts compiles the components with css: \"injected\", which Svelte also adds as <style> elements in the shadow root. A deployer page with Content-Security-Policy style-src 'self' (no 'unsafe-inline', no nonce) blocks both: the launcher, composer and list render unstyled. The clip (bridge/src/clip.ts, modern-screenshot) also loads a data:/blob: image, which an img-src without data:/blob: refuses; the report then files with the clip's error. Not covered by any test.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":41},"content_hash":"372e1f53a6fbeb164e64ed4322735460fe1d25c4f06b198471ddf8a368f045eb"},"suggested_fix":"Adopt the CSS as a constructed stylesheet (new CSSStyleSheet().replaceSync; root.adoptedStyleSheets), compiling the components with css: \"external\" and inlining the emitted CSS into the bundle; add a CSP case with style-src 'self' to web/e2e/queues.spec.ts.","summary":"The overlay's styles are <style> elements in its shadow root, which a page whose CSP style-src lacks 'unsafe-inline' refuses","tags":["csp","overlay","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295779Z","id":"190a6f5dae8aa08534e480442968a7704eb4d175a44fc2e362992b96e36e34c8","body":{"detail":"The poll calls client.myReports() without a cursor and replaces the list with page.reports. A reporter with more reports than the server's page size never sees the older ones, and a reply on one of them does not show.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":134},"end":{"line":139},"content_hash":"71df012d61085aecd4487f7d2c674fb173dd7c961f5250e67cf8684ce38882c7"},"suggested_fix":"Follow next on demand (a Show more button at the list's end), keeping the polled first page merged with the loaded tail by report ID.","summary":"Your reports shows only the first page of myReports; the cursor (next) is never followed","tags":["overlay","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295808Z","id":"127bf81715ef8f5d14c554208c1c67349f64c35523a99462db5f8bcedd94e622","body":{"detail":"The overlay runs in the page's own world (unlike the extension's, web/extension/src/content/overlay-app.ts, which uses closed roots and an extension-page composer). It is open so Playwright can reach it in web/e2e. The page is the deployer's own, which already holds the reporter's session and the auth callback, and the reporter's Ed25519 key is non-extractable (web/sdk/src/sign.ts), so a closed root would add little; a third-party script on that page can read typed text either way.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":36},"end":{"line":36},"content_hash":"2506fc8ee180769cea1d77c3ed518fa3b35075d43268bba807a3dbe05810e5b5"},"summary":"The overlay's shadow root is open, so the page's scripts can read and drive its composer","tags":["overlay","security","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/tokens.css","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T00:07:43.295845Z","id":"023befa6be342664a9bbfae23b216a755c182387ab5f2f7a56bb035a15855be4","body":{"detail":"The overlay cannot import theme.css (its :root rules do not apply in a shadow root and would leak into the page), so tokens.css copies the subset it uses onto :host, light and prefers-color-scheme dark. Nothing checks that the two agree.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":5},"end":{"line":16},"content_hash":"6c9d321dacd1af7ce9d71cb3300dcb297fd8a15fe253de184537ad09491788c9"},"suggested_fix":"Generate tokens.css from theme.css at build time (rewriting :root to :host), or add a unit test that compares each token tokens.css sets with theme.css's value.","summary":"tokens.css repeats the shell's colour tokens by hand; a change to web/shell/src/theme.css does not reach the overlay","tags":["overlay","design-tokens","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/main.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T01:46:30.323873Z","id":"d91b4c0f010b9d3ae5520c66c8ec5fac7f78d00921e27c4b6f8ec8568c2fbdd3","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:4355f90f1","summary":"The overlay's host takes HOST_CSS through host.style.cssText and its shadow root adopts one constructed sheet (web/bridge/src/sheet.ts addSheet) of tokens.css and the components' CSS, which web/vite.overlay.config.ts now writes into overlay.js; no <style> is made where adoptedStyleSheets exists. Evidence: web/e2e/deployer-site/server.ts policyFor now sends style-src 'self' 'report-sample'; bazel test //web:e2e_queues PASSED, asserting .launcher has display:flex and the composer border-top-width 3px under that policy, and that the only violation is modern-screenshot's empty font <style>.","supersedes":"7b5c5fd02200e74ac2224fc033f85d93517f02ed07fe0c118d991bf0277308eb","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:082c8a2e-1d4f-4cb1-8f07-ecd7fd8e2ecf"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:24:03.522165Z","id":"852932cc30ca4760c46a869d0a7f7fc10e35878056a05d0d229965d184461c7a","body":{"detail":"Overlay.svelte makes its picker (overlay/src/picker.ts commentPicker, which appends a CommentMode host <clax-overlay> to <html>, bridge/src/comment-mode.ts:170-179) while the component initialises, and destroys it from onDestroy. Svelte 5 registers an onDestroy teardown through an effect, which runs only once effects flush. When a page calls overlay(...) and then close() on its handle before the next task, unmount finds no teardown: the overlay's own host is removed (main.ts close) but the picker's host and its listeners stay. Seen with the SDK package's bundle (web/sdk/package.test.ts, which waits a task before close for this reason): without the wait, two <clax-overlay> elements are in the page after overlay() and one after close().","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"e99294377d9d8512e61895e922c0f2e1ed6cd39894a2fe8b7f5054392fdca031"},"suggested_fix":"Make the picker in an $effect (or onMount) that returns its destroy, so it exists only once its teardown does; or destroy it in main.ts close() as well as in onDestroy.","summary":"close() in the same task as overlay() leaves comment mode's <clax-overlay> host in the page","tags":["session:claude-code:369633e5-7e93-4e72-b6c2-aedba48817c5"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:06:45.501876Z","id":"983302d7c9d1ea47cedbf6caa81671d6638e2b574e378089e3c5ae97e79c6b32","body":{"detail":"With /_clax/overlay.js a page calls Clax.overlay once. Through @empathic/clax-sdk/overlay an app calls overlay() in a useEffect and close() in its cleanup; React's StrictMode runs one extra setup, cleanup and setup cycle in development (https://react.dev/reference/react/StrictMode), within the same commit, so every such app in development leaves a <clax-overlay> picker host and its listeners behind. web/sdk/package.test.ts:99-101 waits a task before close() to step around this.","kind":"comment","references":"852932cc30ca4760c46a869d0a7f7fc10e35878056a05d0d229965d184461c7a","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":44},"content_hash":"e99294377d9d8512e61895e922c0f2e1ed6cd39894a2fe8b7f5054392fdca031"},"summary":"As an npm import this path is the common case, not an edge: a React app in StrictMode closes the overlay in the task that opened it","tags":["review","review:pr35-sdk-package","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T19:11:00.339624Z","id":"1e11d25a799d5bf7410207e93a47422841c0e3e7ae539e95d69be736326a57c4","body":{"detail":"https://react.dev/reference/react/useEffect (Caveats): 'When Strict Mode is on, React will run one extra development-only setup+cleanup cycle before the first real setup'; Troubleshooting: 'runs setup+cleanup one extra time immediately after component mounts'. https://react.dev/reference/react/StrictMode: development only. React's source, packages/react-reconciler/src/ReactFiberWorkLoop.js at v19.1.0, flushPassiveEffectsImpl calls commitPassiveMountEffects (line 4131) and then, in the same function, `if (__DEV__) commitDoubleInvokeEffectsInDEV(root, true)` (line 4144), so the first setup and the extra cleanup run in one task with no flush of Svelte's effects between. web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte:43-44 makes the picker at init and destroys it in onDestroy; web/overlay/src/main.ts:54-70 mounts with no flushSync and close() calls unmount; web/sdk/package.test.ts:99-101 waits a setTimeout(0) before close(). Scope: development builds only (production runs one setup), so an app in StrictMode leaks one picker host per mount in development.","kind":"comment","references":"983302d7c9d1ea47cedbf6caa81671d6638e2b574e378089e3c5ae97e79c6b32","summary":"confirmed: StrictMode's extra setup/cleanup runs synchronously in the same passive-effects flush, so overlay() then close() land in one task","tags":["verified:confirmed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/overlay/src/Overlay.svelte","issuer":"mailto:benbarber121@gmail.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-29T23:36:12.513299Z","id":"74f59ca65c6c293f1cb549beb47a0f018c8c075de8f56d4f3415dcf6ea9359cb","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:df2fbede","summary":"The picker is now made in onMount, which returns its destroy, so an overlay unmounted before its effects ran never makes it. web/overlay/src/main.test.ts 'leaves nothing in the page when closed in the task that started it' (overlay(opts).close(), no wait) failed before the change ('expected <clax-overlay></clax-overlay> to have a length of +0 but got 1') and passes after under //web:unit; web/sdk/package.test.ts no longer waits a setTimeout(0) before close() and //web:sdk_package passes.","supersedes":"852932cc30ca4760c46a869d0a7f7fc10e35878056a05d0d229965d184461c7a","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:8e745615-4eb7-451a-a3d4-35f6e2615e17"]}}
